  "description": "EMENUI crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H80 Gd4 N6 O19,C2 H6 O1,C2 H3 N1,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.603-5.097 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.21-172.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(μ4-O)(HL3)4(H2L3)2]·3H2O·EtOH·CH3CN (C88H95Gd4N7O23). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
